Bump the workspace version to 0.7.0, the version the changelog already claims

Running `joy --version` printed 0.5.0 while CHANGELOG's top section was 0.7.0:
two rounds of work went out under their own changelog headings without the
version ever moving, so the binary, the MCP `clientInfo` and `joy mcp serve`'s
`serverInfo` all still announced the previous release.

0.7.0 is what the code in the tree is; v0.5.0 stays the last tagged release, and
the Homebrew formula keeps pointing at that tag's archive (a formula pins a
release, it does not float). The changelog heading now says both of those things
so the next person does not have to work it out from `git tag`.

Python SDK follows the same version line.
